/-!
# A closed point of degree `n` of the projective line, as a divisor of class `𝒪(n)`

Let `k` be a field and `K/k` a finite separable extension of degree `n`. The projective bundle
`𝐏(𝒪²) = Proj_{Spec k}(Sym(𝒪²))` of the free module of rank two on `Spec k` is the projective
line `ℙ¹_k`, and `Spec K` sits in it as an effective Cartier divisor in the linear system
`|𝒪(n)|`: if `α` is a primitive element of `K` with minimal polynomial `g` of degree `n`, the
homogenization `G = T₁ⁿ g(T₀ / T₁)` is a section of `𝒪(n)` whose zero scheme is the closed point
`[α : 1]`, with residue field `k(α) = K`.

This is the geometric input that turns the projective bundle axiom (A3) and the divisor axiom
(A4) of Section 45.12 into the nonvanishing of `H^*(Spec K)`: axiom (A4) consumes exactly an
effective Cartier divisor `D` on `𝐏(ℰ)`, an isomorphism of `D` with a smooth projective scheme,
and the class of `𝒪(D)` in the Picard group.

## Main results

* `Stacks.WeilCohomology.exists_effectiveCartierDivisor_isoSpec_picardClassOf_eq`: **there is an
  effective Cartier divisor `D` on `𝐏(𝒪²_{Spec k})` with `D ≅ Spec K` over `Spec k` and
  `[𝒪(D)] = n · [𝒪(1)]` in `Pic(𝐏(𝒪²))`, where `n = [K : k]`.**
* `Stacks.WeilCohomology.ProjectiveLineDegreePoint.bundleIsoProjectiveLine`: the bundle
  `𝐏(𝒪²_{Spec k})` is `Proj k[T₀, T₁]`, over `Spec k`
  (`bundleIsoProjectiveLine_hom_projToSpecCoeff`), with `𝒪(1)` pulling back to the twist of the
  bundle (`nonempty_pullback_bundleIsoProjectiveLine_twistingSheaf`).
* `Stacks.WeilCohomology.ProjectiveLineDegreePoint.pointSchemeIso`: the zero scheme of the
  homogenized minimal polynomial is `Spec K`, over `Spec k` (`pointSchemeIso_hom_comp`).
* `Stacks.WeilCohomology.ProjectiveLineDegreePoint.ker_chartEval`: on the chart
  `D₊(T₁) = Spec k[T₀, T₁]₍T₁₎`, evaluation at `[α : 1]` has kernel generated by `G / T₁ⁿ`.
* `Stacks.WeilCohomology.picardClassOf_pullback_eq_schemePullbackClass`: the Picard class of a
  pulled-back invertible module is the pullback of its Picard class.

## Implementation notes

The comparison `𝐏(𝒪²) ≅ ℙ¹_k` is the composite of three isomorphisms: the chart of the relative
`Proj` over the affine open `⊤` of `Spec k`
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjAffineBase.isIso_chart_top`), the identification of that
chart with `Proj Γ(Spec k, ⊤)[T₀, T₁]` (`Stacks.SymGraded.chartIsoProjPoly`), and the change of
coefficients along `k ≅ Γ(Spec k, ⊤)`. The twists correspond across each of them, so only
`Nonempty` isomorphisms of twists are recorded, which is all a Picard class sees.

The divisor on the bundle is the inverse image of the zero scheme on `ℙ¹_k`; by
`Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_pullback` it is also the zero scheme of the pulled-back section, so
`𝒪(D)` is the pullback of `𝒪(n)`, whose class is `n` times that of `𝒪(1)` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.twistingSheafPicardClass_eq_zsmul`.

The zero scheme lies in the chart `D₊(T₁)`, because `g` is monic: `G ≡ T₀ⁿ` modulo `T₁`. So the
cover map of `Spec(Γ(D₊(T₁)) / I)` into the closed subscheme is an isomorphism, and the ring
`Γ(D₊(T₁)) / I` is computed by dehomogenization, the fraction `a / T₁ᵐ` going to `a(X, 1)`.

The polynomial ring `k[T₀, T₁]` appears both as `Stacks.ProjectiveLine.grading k`, indexed by
`Fin 2`, and as `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjPolyChart.polyGrading k 1`, indexed by
`Fin (1 + 1)`. The two are equal by `rfl`, but rewriting does not see through the difference, so
the proofs restate goals with `change` where they cross from one spelling to the other.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FIS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FIS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FI4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FI4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01OE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OR)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.WeilCohomology.ProjectiveLineDegreePoint

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

open Stacks.SymGraded Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjPolyChart

variable (k : Type u) [Field k]

/-- The free module `𝒪^{n+1}` on a scheme is finite locally free of rank `n + 1`. -/
instance isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_freeModule_coordIndex (X : Scheme.{u}) (n : ℕ) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (freeModule (X := X) (coordIndex.{u} n)) (n + 1) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_free_of_equiv _ (n + 1) Equiv.ulift

/-- The free module `𝒪^{n+1}` on a scheme is finite locally free. -/
instance isFiniteLocallyFree_freeModule_coordIndex (X : Scheme.{u}) (n : ℕ) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u}
      (freeModule (X := X) (coordIndex.{u} n)) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.isFiniteLocallyFree _ (n + 1)

/-- The free module `𝒪²` of rank two on `Spec k`. -/
abbrev freeRankTwo : (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)).Modules :=
  freeModule (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (coordIndex.{u} 1)

/-- The chart of `𝐏(𝒪²)` over the affine open `⊤` of `Spec k`. -/
def topChart : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj ((freeSymGradedAlgebra (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k))
    (coordIndex.{u} 1)).grading ⊤) ⟶ Stacks.Chow.bundle (freeRankTwo k) :=
  (relativeProj (freeSymGradedAlgebra (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k))
    (coordIndex.{u} 1))).chart ⊤ (isAffineOpen_top (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)))

/-- Over an affine base the chart over `⊤` is an isomorphism. -/
instance isIso_topChart : IsIso (topChart k) :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjAffineBase.isIso_chart_top _
    (isAffineOpen_top (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)))

/-- The ring of global functions of `Spec k`, in the spelling of the chart comparison, is `k`. -/
def coeffEquiv : k ≃+* ↥(siteRing (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (op ⊤)) :=
  (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of k)).symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

/-- Change of coefficients `k[T₀, T₁] ⟶ Γ(Spec k, ⊤)[T₀, T₁]`, a graded ring isomorphism. -/
abbrev coeffHom : polyGrading k 1 →+*ᵍ
    polyGrading ↥(siteRing (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (op ⊤)) 1 :=
  coeffGradedHom k 1 (coeffEquiv k).toRingHom

/-- The inverse change of coefficients. -/
abbrev coeffInvHom : polyGrading ↥(siteRing (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (op ⊤)) 1 →+*ᵍ
    polyGrading k 1 :=
  coeffGradedHom _ 1 (coeffEquiv k).symm.toRingHom

/-- The coefficient change along the inverse of a ring isomorphism undoes the one along it. -/
private theorem coeffGradedHom_symm_comp {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (e : R ≃+* S) :
    (coeffGradedHom S 1 e.symm.toRingHom).comp (coeffGradedHom R 1 e.toRingHom) =
      GradedRingHom.id _ :=
  GradedRingHom.ext fun F => by
    change MvPolynomial.map _ (MvPolynomial.map _ F) = F
    rw [MvPolynomial.map_map]
    simp only [RingEquiv.toRingHom_eq_coe, RingEquiv.symm_comp]
    exact MvPolynomial.map_id F

/-- The two changes of coefficients compose to the identity of `k[T₀, T₁]`. -/
theorem coeffInvHom_comp_coeffHom : (coeffInvHom k).comp (coeffHom k) = GradedRingHom.id _ :=
  coeffGradedHom_symm_comp (coeffEquiv k)

/-- The two changes of coefficients compose to the identity of `Γ(Spec k, ⊤)[T₀, T₁]`. -/
theorem coeffHom_comp_coeffInvHom : (coeffHom k).comp (coeffInvHom k) = GradedRingHom.id _ :=
  coeffGradedHom_symm_comp (coeffEquiv k).symm

/-- `Proj Γ(Spec k, ⊤)[T₀, T₁] ≅ Proj k[T₀, T₁]`, by change of coefficients. -/
def coeffProjIso :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading ↥(siteRing (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (op ⊤)) 1) ≅
      projectiveLineProj k :=
  haveI : IsIso (Proj.map (coeffHom k) (irrelevant_le_map_coeffGradedHom k 1 _)) :=
    Proj.isIso_map _ (irrelevant_le_map_coeffGradedHom _ 1 _) (coeffInvHom_comp_coeffHom k)
      (coeffHom_comp_coeffInvHom k)
  asIso (Proj.map (coeffHom k) (irrelevant_le_map_coeffGradedHom k 1 _))

/-- **The projective bundle of `𝒪²` on `Spec k` is the projective line** `Proj k[T₀, T₁]`. -/
def bundleIsoProjectiveLine : Stacks.Chow.bundle (freeRankTwo k) ≅ projectiveLineProj k :=
  (asIso (topChart k)).symm ≪≫ chartIsoProjPoly (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) 1 ⊤ ≪≫
    coeffProjIso k

/-- The degree-zero part of a constant polynomial is that constant. -/
theorem projZero_C {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (r : R) :
    ((GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (polyGrading R 1) (MvPolynomial.C r) : polyGrading R 1 0) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin (1 + 1)) R) = MvPolynomial.C r := by
  rw [GradedRing.coe_projZeroRingHom'_apply, GradedRing.projZeroRingHom_apply]
  exact DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same _
    (MvPolynomial.C_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_zero (Fin (1 + 1)) R r)

/-- The coefficient comparison as a morphism of commutative rings. -/
abbrev coeffRingHom : CommRingCat.of k ⟶
    CommRingCat.of ↥(siteRing (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (op ⊤)) :=
  CommRingCat.ofHom (coeffEquiv k).toRingHom

/-- The change of coefficients is compatible with the structure morphisms. -/
theorem coeffProjIso_hom_projToSpecCoeff :
    (coeffProjIso k).hom ≫ projToSpecCoeff k 1 =
      projToSpecCoeff ↥(siteRing (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (op ⊤)) 1 ≫
        Spec.map (coeffRingHom k) := by
  simp only [coeffProjIso, asIso_hom, projToSpecCoeff, Category.assoc,
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map_toSpecZero_assoc, ← Spec.map_comp]
  refine congrArg (fun φ => Proj.toSpecZero _ ≫ Spec.map φ) ?_
  refine CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun r => Subtype.ext ?_)
  change MvPolynomial.map (coeffEquiv k).toRingHom
      ((GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (polyGrading k 1) (MvPolynomial.C r) : polyGrading k 1 0) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin (1 + 1)) k) =
    ((GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (polyGrading ↥(siteRing (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (op ⊤)) 1)
      (MvPolynomial.C ((coeffEquiv k) r))) : MvPolynomial (Fin (1 + 1)) _)
  rw [projZero_C, projZero_C, MvPolynomial.map_C]
  rfl

/-- The inclusion of `⊤` into `Spec k`, through the affine identification of `⊤`. -/
theorem top_ι_eq : (⊤ : (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)).Opens).ι =
    (isAffineOpen_top (Spec (CommRingCat.of k))).isoSpec.hom ≫ Spec.map (coeffRingHom k) := by
  rw [← Iso.inv_comp_eq, IsAffineOpen.isoSpec_inv_ι]
  exact IsAffineOpen.fromSpec_top.trans (Scheme.isoSpec_Spec_inv _)

/-- **The comparison `𝐏(𝒪²) ≅ ℙ¹_k` is over `Spec k`.** -/
theorem bundleIsoProjectiveLine_hom_projToSpecCoeff :
    (bundleIsoProjectiveLine k).hom ≫ projToSpecCoeff k 1 =
      Stacks.Chow.bundleProj (freeRankTwo k) := by
  have h1 := chartIsoProjPoly_hom_comp_projToSpecCoeff (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) 1 ⊤
    (isAffineOpen_top (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)))
  have h3 := ((relativeProj (freeSymGradedAlgebra (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k))
    (coordIndex.{u} 1))).chart_isPullback ⊤ (isAffineOpen_top (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)))).w
  simp only [bundleIsoProjectiveLine, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, asIso_inv, Category.assoc,
    coeffProjIso_hom_projToSpecCoeff]
  rw [IsIso.inv_comp_eq]
  exact (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans ((congrArg (· ≫ Spec.map (coeffRingHom k)) h1).trans
    ((Category.assoc _ _ _).trans ((congrArg (fun φ => projInclusionToOpen _ ⊤
      (isAffineOpen_top (Spec (CommRingCat.of k))) ≫ φ) (top_ι_eq k).symm).trans h3.symm)))

open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj in
/-- The twists correspond across the change of coefficients. -/
theorem nonempty_pullback_coeffProjIso_hom_twistingSheaf (m : ℤ) :
    Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (coeffProjIso k).hom).obj
        (twistingSheafModule (polyGrading k 1) m) ≅
      twistingSheafModule (polyGrading ↥(siteRing (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (op ⊤)) 1) m) :=
  Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.nonempty_pullbackTwist_projMap _ _ (coeffHom k)
    (irrelevant_le_map_coeffGradedHom k 1 _)
    (MvPolynomial.map_surjective _ (coeffEquiv k).surjective)
    (MvPolynomial.adjoin_homogeneousSubmodule_one_eq_top (Fin (1 + 1)) k) m

open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj in
/-- The twist of the bundle restricts to `𝒪(1)` on the chart over `⊤`. -/
def topChartTwistIso :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback (topChart k)).obj (Stacks.Chow.bundleTwist (freeRankTwo k)) ≅
      twistingSheaf ((freeSymGradedAlgebra (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k))
        (coordIndex.{u} 1)).grading ⊤) 1 :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwistChartBridge.chartPieceIso
    (projectiveBundleTwistData (freeRankTwo k) (Stacks.Chow.bundlePieces (freeRankTwo k))) ⊤
    (isAffineOpen_top (Spec (CommRingCat.of k))) 1

open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj in
/-- **`𝒪(1)` on `ℙ¹_k` pulls back to the twist `𝒪_{𝐏(𝒪²)}(1)` of the bundle.** -/
theorem nonempty_pullback_bundleIsoProjectiveLine_twistingSheaf :
    Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (bundleIsoProjectiveLine k).hom).obj
        (twistingSheafModule (polyGrading k 1) 1) ≅ Stacks.Chow.bundleTwist (freeRankTwo k)) := by
  obtain ⟨β⟩ := nonempty_pullback_coeffProjIso_hom_twistingSheaf k 1
  obtain ⟨γ⟩ := nonempty_pullback_chartIsoProjPoly_hom_twistingSheaf
    (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) 1 ⊤ 1
  obtain ⟨δ⟩ := nonempty_pullback_inv_of_pullback_hom (asIso (topChart k))
    (Stacks.Chow.bundleTwist (freeRankTwo k)) _ ⟨topChartTwistIso k⟩
  refine ⟨?_⟩
  refine ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp _ _).app _).symm ≪≫ ?_
  refine (Scheme.Modules.pullback (asIso (topChart k)).inv).mapIso
    (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp _ _).app _).symm ≪≫
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback _).mapIso β ≪≫ γ) ≪≫ δ

/-! ### The chart ring `k[T₀, T₁]₍T₁₎` -/

section Algebra

open Stacks.ProjectiveLine

variable {k}

/-- Dehomogenization sends `T₁` to a unit. -/
theorem isUnit_dehomogenize_X_one :
    IsUnit ((dehomogenize k).toRingHom (MvPolynomial.X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)) := by
  simp

/-- Dehomogenization on the chart ring `k[T₀, T₁]₍T₁₎`: the fraction `a / T₁ ^ m` goes to the
dehomogenization of `a`. -/
def chartDehom :
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X 1) →+* Polynomial k :=
  (IsLocalization.Away.lift (R := MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)
    (S := Localization.Away (MvPolynomial.X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k))
    (MvPolynomial.X 1) (isUnit_dehomogenize_X_one (k := k))).comp
    (algebraMap (HomogeneousLocalization.Away (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X 1))
      (Localization.Away (MvPolynomial.X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)))

/-- `chartDehom` on a fraction `a / T₁ ^ m`. -/
theorem chartDehom_mk (m : ℕ) (a : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)
    (ha : a ∈ ProjectiveLine.grading k (m • 1)) :
    chartDehom (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk _
      (mem_grading (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_X k 1)) m a ha) = dehomogenize k a := by
  rw [chartDehom, RingHom.comp_apply, HomogeneousLocalization.algebraMap_apply,
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk, Localization.mk_eq_mk']
  refine (IsLocalization.lift_mk'_spec _ _ _ _).mpr ?_
  simp

/-- A member of the graded piece of degree `m • 1` is a form of degree `m`. -/
theorem isHomogeneous_of_mem_grading {m : ℕ} {a : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k}
    (ha : a ∈ ProjectiveLine.grading k (m • 1)) : a.IsHomogeneous m := by
  simpa [smul_eq_mul] using (MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 ha

/-- The degree-`m` homogenization lies in the graded piece of degree `m • 1`. -/
theorem homogenize_mem_grading (p : Polynomial k) (m : ℕ) :
    p.homogenize m ∈ ProjectiveLine.grading k (m • 1) :=
  (MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).2 (by
    rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_one]
    exact Polynomial.isHomogeneous_homogenize p)

/-- The chart fraction `p^{(m)} / T₁ ^ m` of the degree-`m` homogenization of `p`. -/
abbrev homogenizeFraction (p : Polynomial k) (m : ℕ) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X 1) :=
  HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk _ (mem_grading (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_X k 1)) m
    (p.homogenize m) (homogenize_mem_grading p m)

/-- Dehomogenization undoes homogenization on the chart ring. -/
theorem chartDehom_homogenizeFraction (p : Polynomial k) {m : ℕ} (hm : p.natDegree ≤ m) :
    chartDehom (homogenizeFraction p m) = p := by
  rw [chartDehom_mk, dehomogenize_homogenize hm]

/-- Dehomogenization on the chart ring is surjective. -/
theorem chartDehom_surjective : Function.Surjective (chartDehom (k := k)) := fun p =>
  ⟨homogenizeFraction p p.natDegree, chartDehom_homogenizeFraction p le_rfl⟩

/-- A fraction `a / T₁ ^ m` whose dehomogenization is divisible by the monic polynomial `g` is a
multiple of `g^{(deg g)} / T₁ ^ {deg g}`. -/
theorem mk_mem_span_of_dvd_dehomogenize {g : Polynomial k} (hg : g.Monic) (m : ℕ)
    (a : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) (ha : a ∈ ProjectiveLine.grading k (m • 1))
    (hdvd : g ∣ dehomogenize k a) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk _ (mem_grading (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_X k 1)) m a ha ∈
      Ideal.span {homogenizeFraction g g.natDegree} := by
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := hdvd
  have ha' := isHomogeneous_of_mem_grading ha
  by_cases hq0 : q = 0
  · have ha0 : a = 0 := by
      rw [← dehomogenize_eq_zero_iff ha', hq, hq0, mul_zero]
    subst ha0
    convert Ideal.zero_mem _
    exact HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective _ (by
      rw [HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk, HomogeneousLocalization.val_zero,
        Localization.mk_zero])
  · have hdeg : g.natDegree + q.natDegree ≤ m := by
      rw [← hg.natDegree_mul' hq0, ← hq]
      exact natDegree_dehomogenize_le ha'
    obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ : ∃ r, m = g.natDegree + r := ⟨m - g.natDegree, by omega⟩
    have hqr : q.natDegree ≤ r := by omega
    have haGQ : a = g.homogenize g.natDegree * q.homogenize r := by
      rw [← homogenize_dehomogenize ha', hq, Polynomial.homogenize_mul g q le_rfl hqr]
    subst haGQ
    have hmul : HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk _ (mem_grading (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_X k 1))
        (g.natDegree + r) _ ha =
        homogenizeFraction g g.natDegree * homogenizeFraction q r := by
      refine HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective _ ?_
      rw [HomogeneousLocalization.val_mul, HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk,
        HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk, HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk,
        Localization.mk_mul]
      congr 1
      exact Subtype.ext (pow_add _ _ _)
    rw [hmul]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)

/-- **The ideal of the chart ring generated by a homogenized monic polynomial** `g` consists of the
elements whose dehomogenization is divisible by `g`. -/
theorem mem_span_homogenizeFraction_iff {g : Polynomial k} (hg : g.Monic)
    (x : HomogeneousLocalization.Away (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X 1)) :
    x ∈ Ideal.span {homogenizeFraction g g.natDegree} ↔ g ∣ chartDehom x := by
  constructor
  · intro hx
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 hx
    rw [map_mul, chartDehom_homogenizeFraction g le_rfl]
    exact dvd_mul_left _ _
  · intro hx
    obtain ⟨m, a, ha, rfl⟩ := HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk_surjective _
      (mem_grading (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_X k 1)) x
    rw [chartDehom_mk] at hx
    exact mk_mem_span_of_dvd_dehomogenize hg m a ha hx

variable {K : Type u} [Field K] [Algebra k K] (pb : PowerBasis k K)

/-- Evaluation at the point `[α : 1]` on the chart ring, for `α` the generator of a power
basis. -/
def chartEval :
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X 1) →+* K :=
  (Polynomial.aeval pb.gen).toRingHom.comp chartDehom

/-- Evaluation at `[α : 1]` is surjective, `α` generating `K`. -/
theorem chartEval_surjective : Function.Surjective (chartEval pb) := fun y => by
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := pb.exists_eq_aeval' y
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := chartDehom_surjective p
  exact ⟨x, by rw [chartEval, RingHom.comp_apply, hx]; rfl⟩

/-- **The kernel of evaluation at `[α : 1]`** is generated by the homogenized minimal polynomial
of `α`, divided by the corresponding power of `T₁`. -/
theorem ker_chartEval : RingHom.ker (chartEval pb) =
    Ideal.span {homogenizeFraction (minpoly k pb.gen) (minpoly k pb.gen).natDegree} := by
  ext x
  rw [mem_span_homogenizeFraction_iff (minpoly.monic pb.isIntegral_gen), minpoly.dvd_iff,
    RingHom.mem_ker]
  rfl

end Algebra

/-! ### Pullback of Picard classes -/

/-- `Stacks.WeilCohomology.picardClassOf` of a pullback is the pullback of the Picard class. -/
theorem _root_.Stacks.WeilCohomology.picardClassOf_pullback_eq_schemePullbackClass
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) (L : Y.Modules)
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.presheaf Y.ringCatSheaf.2 L)
    (hL' : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.toRingedSpace.presheaf
      (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureIsSheaf Y.toRingedSpace) L) :
    picardClassOf X ((Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj L) (isInvertible_pullback_obj f L hL) =
      Stacks.Picard.schemePullbackClass f
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass _ _ L hL') := by
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (Stacks.Picard.pullbackClass_classOf f.toLRSHom.toShHom L hL').symm
  exact (Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_eq_iff _ _ _ _ _ _).2
    ⟨(Stacks.ProjectiveBundleQuotients.pullbackIso f).app L⟩

/-- The class of `𝒪(D)` only depends on the divisor. -/
theorem picardClassOf_divisorSheaf_congr {X : Scheme.{u}} {D D' : X.IdealSheafData} (h : D = D')
    [Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D] [Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D'] :
    picardClassOf X (Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheaf D) (Stacks.Divisors.isInvertible_divisorSheaf D) =
      picardClassOf X (Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheaf D')
        (Stacks.Divisors.isInvertible_divisorSheaf D') := by
  subst h
  rfl

section Geometry

open ProjectiveLine AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj Stacks.ProjChartBasicOpen

/-! ### The closed point of `ℙ¹_k` cut out by the minimal polynomial -/

/-- The standard chart `D₊(Tᵢ)` of `ℙ¹_k` as an affine open. -/
abbrev chart (i : Fin 2) : (projectiveLineProj k).affineOpens :=
  ⟨Proj.basicOpen (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X i),
    Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen _ _ (X_mem_one k 1 i) one_pos⟩

variable {k} {K : Type u} [Field K] [Algebra k K] (pb : PowerBasis k K)

/-- The degree of the minimal polynomial of the generator. -/
abbrev deg : ℕ := (minpoly k pb.gen).natDegree

/-- The homogenized minimal polynomial, a binary form of degree `deg pb`. -/
abbrev minpolyForm : ProjectiveLine.grading k (deg pb • 1) :=
  ⟨(minpoly k pb.gen).homogenize (deg pb), homogenize_mem_grading _ _⟩

/-- The twist `𝒪(deg pb)` of `ℙ¹_k`. -/
abbrev degreeTwist : (projectiveLineProj k).Modules :=
  twistingSheafModule (ProjectiveLine.grading k) ((deg pb • 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)

/-- The section of `𝒪(deg pb)` attached to the homogenized minimal polynomial. -/
abbrev minpolySection : Γ(degreeTwist pb, ⊤) :=
  degreeSection (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (deg pb • 1) (minpolyForm pb)

/-- **The closed point of `ℙ¹_k` cut out by the homogenized minimal polynomial**, as the zero
scheme of the corresponding section of `𝒪(deg pb)`. -/
abbrev pointScheme : (projectiveLineProj k).IdealSheafData :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme (projectiveLineProj k) (degreeTwist pb) (minpolySection pb)

/-- The homogenized minimal polynomial vanishes at every point of the support of its zero scheme,
read on a standard chart. -/
theorem notMem_basicOpen_minpolyForm_of_mem_support (i : Fin 2)
    {x : projectiveLineProj k} (hx : x ∈ (pointScheme pb).support)
    (hi : x ∈ Proj.basicOpen (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X i)) :
    x ∉ Proj.basicOpen (ProjectiveLine.grading k)
      ((minpolyForm pb : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)) := by
  intro hG
  have h := (Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem (U := chart k i) hi).1 hx
  rw [zeroScheme_degreeSection_ideal_basicOpen _ (X_mem_one k 1 i) one_pos (deg pb)
    (minpolyForm pb), Scheme.zeroLocus_span, Scheme.zeroLocus_singleton] at h
  have h' : x ∉ (projectiveLineProj k).basicOpen ((Proj.awayToSection _ _).hom
      (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk _ (X_mem_one k 1 i) (deg pb) _ (minpolyForm pb).2)) := h
  rw [basicOpen_awayToSection_mk _ _ one_pos] at h'
  exact h' ⟨hi, hG⟩

/-- **The closed point lies in the chart `D₊(T₁)`**: the minimal polynomial is monic, so its
homogenization is `T₀ⁿ` modulo `T₁`. -/
theorem mem_basicOpen_X_one_of_mem_support {x : projectiveLineProj k}
    (hx : x ∈ (pointScheme pb).support) :
    x ∈ Proj.basicOpen (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X 1) := by
  by_contra h1
  have hcov : x ∈ (⨆ i : Fin (1 + 1),
      Proj.basicOpen (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (1 + 1)) k) (MvPolynomial.X i)) := by
    rw [Stacks.ProjectiveChart.iSup_basicOpen_X_eq_top]; trivial
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.1 hcov
  have h0 : x ∈ Proj.basicOpen (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X 0) := by
    fin_cases i
    · exact hi
    · exact absurd hi h1
  have hG := notMem_basicOpen_minpolyForm_of_mem_support pb 0 hx h0
  rw [Proj.mem_basicOpen, not_not] at hG h1
  rw [Proj.mem_basicOpen] at h0
  have hhom : ((minpolyForm pb : ProjectiveLine.grading k (deg pb • 1)) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k).IsHomogeneous (deg pb) :=
    isHomogeneous_of_mem_grading (minpolyForm pb).2
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := X_one_dvd_sub_C_mul_X_zero_pow hhom
  have hc : (dehomogenize k ((minpolyForm pb : ProjectiveLine.grading k (deg pb • 1)) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)).coeff (deg pb) = 1 := by
    change (dehomogenize k ((minpoly k pb.gen).homogenize (deg pb))).coeff (deg pb) = 1
    rw [dehomogenize_homogenize le_rfl]
    exact minpoly.monic pb.isIntegral_gen
  rw [hc, map_one, one_mul] at hw
  have hX0 : (MvPolynomial.X 0 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) ^ deg pb ∈
      x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal := by
    have : (MvPolynomial.X 0 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) ^ deg pb =
        ((minpolyForm pb : ProjectiveLine.grading k (deg pb • 1)) : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) -
          MvPolynomial.X 1 * w := by rw [← hw]; ring
    rw [this]
    exact Ideal.sub_mem _ hG (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ h1)
  exact h0 (x.isPrime.mem_of_pow_mem _ hX0)

/-- The closed subscheme lies over the chart `D₊(T₁)`. -/
theorem preimage_chart_one_eq_top :
    (pointScheme pb).subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ (chart k 1).1 = ⊤ :=
  top_unique fun z _ => mem_basicOpen_X_one_of_mem_support pb (by
    have hz : (pointScheme pb).subschemeι z ∈ Set.range (pointScheme pb).subschemeι := ⟨z, rfl⟩
    rwa [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι] at hz)

/-- The chart of the closed subscheme over `D₊(T₁)` is all of it. -/
instance isIso_subschemeCover_f_chart_one :
    IsIso ((pointScheme pb).subschemeCover.f (chart k 1)) :=
  haveI : IsOpenImmersion ((pointScheme pb).subschemeCover.f (chart k 1)) :=
    (pointScheme pb).subschemeCover.map_prop _
  isIso_of_isOpenImmersion_of_opensRange_eq_top _
    ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.opensRange_subschemeCover_map _ _).trans
      (preimage_chart_one_eq_top pb))

variable (k) in
/-- The ring of functions on the chart `D₊(T₁)` is the chart ring. -/
def chartSectionsEquiv : HomogeneousLocalization.Away (ProjectiveLine.grading k)
    (MvPolynomial.X 1) ≃+* Γ(projectiveLineProj k, (chart k 1).1) :=
  (Proj.basicOpenIsoAway (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X 1) (X_mem_one k 1 1)
    one_pos).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

/-- Evaluation at the closed point on the functions on `D₊(T₁)`. -/
def sectionsEval : Γ(projectiveLineProj k, (chart k 1).1) →+* K :=
  (chartEval pb).comp (chartSectionsEquiv k).symm.toRingHom

/-- Evaluation at the closed point is surjective. -/
theorem sectionsEval_surjective : Function.Surjective (sectionsEval pb) :=
  (chartEval_surjective pb).comp (chartSectionsEquiv k).symm.surjective

/-- The kernel of evaluation at the closed point is the ideal of the closed subscheme. -/
theorem ker_sectionsEval :
    RingHom.ker (sectionsEval pb) = (pointScheme pb).ideal (chart k 1) := by
  rw [zeroScheme_degreeSection_ideal_basicOpen _ (X_mem_one k 1 1) one_pos (deg pb)
    (minpolyForm pb)]
  calc RingHom.ker (sectionsEval pb)
      = (RingHom.ker (chartEval pb)).comap (chartSectionsEquiv k).symm :=
        (RingHom.comap_ker _ _).symm
    _ = (RingHom.ker (chartEval pb)).map (chartSectionsEquiv k) := Ideal.comap_symm _
    _ = _ := by rw [ker_chartEval, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]; rfl

/-- The ring of functions of the closed point is `K`. -/
def quotEquiv :
    Γ(projectiveLineProj k, (chart k 1).1) ⧸ (pointScheme pb).ideal (chart k 1) ≃+* K :=
  (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (ker_sectionsEval pb).symm).trans
    (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (sectionsEval_surjective pb))

/-- `quotEquiv` is evaluation at the closed point. -/
theorem quotEquiv_mk (y : Γ(projectiveLineProj k, (chart k 1).1)) :
    quotEquiv pb (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ y) = sectionsEval pb y := rfl

/-- **The closed point is `Spec K`.** -/
def pointSchemeIso : (pointScheme pb).subscheme ≅ Spec (CommRingCat.of K) :=
  (asIso ((pointScheme pb).subschemeCover.f (chart k 1))).symm ≪≫
    Scheme.Spec.mapIso (quotEquiv pb).symm.toCommRingCatIso.op

/-- Dehomogenization on the image of a degree-zero element. -/
theorem chartDehom_fromZeroRingHom (a : ProjectiveLine.grading k 0) :
    chartDehom (HomogeneousLocalization.fromZeroRingHom _ _ a) = dehomogenize k a := by
  rw [chartDehom, RingHom.comp_apply, HomogeneousLocalization.algebraMap_apply]
  change IsLocalization.Away.lift _ _ (Localization.mk (a : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) 1) = _
  rw [Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap, IsLocalization.Away.lift_eq]
  rfl

/-- `quotEquiv` is a `k`-algebra map: a constant goes to its image in `K`. -/
theorem quotEquiv_mk_constant (r : k) :
    quotEquiv pb (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ ((Proj.awayToSection (ProjectiveLine.grading k)
      (MvPolynomial.X 1)).hom (HomogeneousLocalization.fromZeroRingHom _ _
        ((GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (polyGrading k 1)).comp
          (algebraMap k (MvPolynomial (Fin (1 + 1)) k)) r)))) = algebraMap k K r := by
  rw [quotEquiv_mk, sectionsEval, RingHom.comp_apply]
  change chartEval pb ((chartSectionsEquiv k).symm (chartSectionsEquiv k _)) = _
  rw [RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply, chartEval, RingHom.comp_apply, chartDehom_fromZeroRingHom]
  change Polynomial.aeval pb.gen (dehomogenize k ((GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (polyGrading k 1)
    (MvPolynomial.C r) : polyGrading k 1 0) : MvPolynomial (Fin (1 + 1)) k)) = _
  rw [projZero_C]
  simp

/-- **The isomorphism of the closed point with `Spec K` is over `Spec k`.** -/
theorem pointSchemeIso_hom_comp :
    (pointSchemeIso pb).hom ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)) =
      (pointScheme pb).subschemeι ≫ projToSpecCoeff k 1 := by
  rw [pointSchemeIso, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, asIso_inv, Category.assoc, IsIso.inv_comp_eq,
    ← Category.assoc, Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeCover_map_subschemeι,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.glueDataObjι_ι,
    ← SpecMap_awayToSection_awayι _ (X_mem_one k 1 1) one_pos]
  change Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (quotEquiv pb).symm.toRingHom) ≫
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)) =
    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk ((pointScheme pb).ideal (chart k 1)))) ≫
      Spec.map (Proj.awayToSection (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X 1)) ≫
        Proj.awayι (ProjectiveLine.grading k) (MvPolynomial.X 1) (X_mem_one k 1 1) one_pos) ≫
      Proj.toSpecZero (ProjectiveLine.grading k) ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        ((GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (ProjectiveLine.grading k)).comp
          (algebraMap k (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k))))
  rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, Proj.awayι_toSpecZero_assoc, ← Spec.map_comp,
    ← Spec.map_comp, ← Spec.map_comp, ← Spec.map_comp]
  refine congrArg Spec.map (CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun r => ?_))
  apply (quotEquiv pb).injective
  change quotEquiv pb ((quotEquiv pb).symm (algebraMap k K r)) = _
  rw [RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  exact (quotEquiv_mk_constant pb r).symm

/-- The section of `𝒪(n)` attached to the homogenized minimal polynomial is nonzero. -/
theorem minpolySection_ne_zero : minpolySection pb ≠ 0 :=
  Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.degreeSection_ne_zero k 1 (deg pb • 1) (minpolyForm pb)
    (fun h => (minpoly.ne_zero pb.isIntegral_gen) (by
      have := congrArg (dehomogenize k) h
      rwa [map_zero, dehomogenize_homogenize le_rfl] at this))

/-- The global section `minpolySection pb`, read as a section of the module sheaf. -/
abbrev minpolySections : (degreeTwist pb).sections :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTopOfRingSheaf _ (minpolySection pb)

/-- The closed point is the zero scheme of the section, read as a section of the module sheaf. -/
theorem pointScheme_eq : pointScheme pb =
    AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme (projectiveLineProj k) (degreeTwist pb)
      ((minpolySections pb).eval (op ⊤)) :=
  congrArg (AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme (projectiveLineProj k) (degreeTwist pb))
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTopOfRingSheaf_eval_top (degreeTwist pb)
      (minpolySection pb)).symm

/-- **The closed point is an effective Cartier divisor**, `ℙ¹_k` being integral. -/
instance isEffectiveCartierDivisor_pointScheme :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (pointScheme pb) := by
  rw [pointScheme_eq]
  exact Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_zeroScheme_of_eval_top_ne_zero _ _ _
    (fun h => minpolySection_ne_zero pb
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTopOfRingSheaf_eval_top (degreeTwist pb)
        (minpolySection pb)).symm.trans h))

end Geometry

/-! ### Transport to the projective bundle -/

section Bundle

open ProjectiveLine AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj

variable {k} {K : Type u} [Field K] [Algebra k K] (pb : PowerBasis k K)

variable (k) in
/-- **`𝒪(m)` on `ℙ¹_k` pulls back to `m` times the twist of the bundle** in `Pic(𝐏(𝒪²))`. -/
theorem picardClassOf_pullback_twistingSheaf (m : ℤ) :
    picardClassOf _ ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (bundleIsoProjectiveLine k).hom).obj
        (twistingSheafModule (ProjectiveLine.grading k) m))
        (isInvertible_pullback_obj _ _ inferInstance) =
      m • picardClassOf _ (Stacks.Chow.bundleTwist (freeRankTwo k))
        (Stacks.Chow.isInvertible_bundleTwist (freeRankTwo k)) := by
  rw [picardClassOf_pullback_eq_schemePullbackClass _ _ inferInstance
    (isInvertible_twistingSheaf_projectiveLineProj k m)]
  change Stacks.Picard.schemePullbackClassHom (bundleIsoProjectiveLine k).hom
    (twistingSheafPicardClass k m) = _
  rw [twistingSheafPicardClass_eq_zsmul, map_zsmul, Stacks.Picard.schemePullbackClassHom,
    Stacks.Picard.pullbackClassHom_apply]
  congr 1
  obtain ⟨β⟩ := nonempty_pullback_bundleIsoProjectiveLine_twistingSheaf k
  refine (picardClassOf_pullback_eq_schemePullbackClass _ _ inferInstance
    (isInvertible_twistingSheaf_projectiveLineProj k 1)).symm.trans ?_
  exact picardClassOf_eq_of_iso _ _ _ _ _ β

/-- The divisor on `𝐏(𝒪²)` corresponding to the closed point `pointScheme pb` of `ℙ¹_k`. -/
abbrev bundleDivisor : (Stacks.Chow.bundle (freeRankTwo k)).IdealSheafData :=
  (pointScheme pb).comap (bundleIsoProjectiveLine k).hom

/-- The divisor on the bundle is an effective Cartier divisor. -/
instance isEffectiveCartierDivisor_bundleDivisor :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (bundleDivisor pb) :=
  Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_of_isOpenImmersion _ inferInstance _

/-- The divisor is `Spec K`. -/
def bundleDivisorIso : (bundleDivisor pb).subscheme ≅ Spec (CommRingCat.of K) :=
  (pointScheme pb).comapIso _ ≪≫ asIso (pullback.snd _ _) ≪≫ pointSchemeIso pb

/-- The isomorphism of the divisor with `Spec K` is over `Spec k`. -/
theorem bundleDivisorIso_hom_comp :
    (bundleDivisorIso pb).hom ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)) =
      (bundleDivisor pb).subschemeι ≫ Stacks.Chow.bundleProj (freeRankTwo k) := by
  rw [bundleDivisorIso, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.trans_hom, asIso_hom, Category.assoc, Category.assoc,
    pointSchemeIso_hom_comp, ← pullback.condition_assoc, ← Scheme.IdealSheafData.comapIso_hom_fst,
    Category.assoc, bundleIsoProjectiveLine_hom_projToSpecCoeff]

/-- The divisor on the bundle is the zero scheme of the pulled-back section. -/
theorem bundleDivisor_eq : bundleDivisor pb =
    AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme (Stacks.Chow.bundle (freeRankTwo k))
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (bundleIsoProjectiveLine k).hom).obj (degreeTwist pb))
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTopOfRingSheaf _ (pullbackGlobalSections
        (bundleIsoProjectiveLine k).hom (degreeTwist pb) (minpolySection pb))).eval (op ⊤)) :=
  (Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_pullback _ _ _).symm.trans
    (congrArg (AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme _ _)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTopOfRingSheaf_eval_top _ _).symm)

/-- **The class of `𝒪(D)` is `n` times the class of the twist.** -/
theorem picardClassOf_divisorSheaf_bundleDivisor :
    picardClassOf _ (Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheaf (bundleDivisor pb))
        (Stacks.Divisors.isInvertible_divisorSheaf _) =
      ((deg pb • 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) • picardClassOf _ (Stacks.Chow.bundleTwist (freeRankTwo k))
        (Stacks.Chow.isInvertible_bundleTwist (freeRankTwo k)) := by
  have hD' : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme
      (Stacks.Chow.bundle (freeRankTwo k))
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (bundleIsoProjectiveLine k).hom).obj (degreeTwist pb))
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTopOfRingSheaf _ (pullbackGlobalSections
        (bundleIsoProjectiveLine k).hom (degreeTwist pb) (minpolySection pb))).eval (op ⊤))) :=
    (bundleDivisor_eq pb) ▸ isEffectiveCartierDivisor_bundleDivisor pb
  refine (@picardClassOf_divisorSheaf_congr _ _ _ (bundleDivisor_eq pb) _ hD').trans ?_
  refine (@FirstChernClassData.picardClassOf_divisorSheaf_zeroScheme _ _ _ _ hD').trans ?_
  exact picardClassOf_pullback_twistingSheaf k _

end Bundle

end Stacks.WeilCohomology.ProjectiveLineDegreePoint

namespace Stacks.WeilCohomology

open ProjectiveLineDegreePoint

variable (k : Type u) [Field k]

/-- **A finite separable extension `K/k` of degree `n` is a divisor of class `𝒪(n)` on `ℙ¹_k`.**
Let `ℰ = 𝒪²` be the free module of rank two on `Spec k`, so that its projective bundle
`π : 𝐏(ℰ) ⟶ Spec k` is the projective line. There is an effective Cartier divisor `D ⊆ 𝐏(ℰ)`
together with an isomorphism `D ≅ Spec K` over `Spec k`, whose invertible module `𝒪(D)` has class
`n · [𝒪_{𝐏(ℰ)}(1)]` in `Pic(𝐏(ℰ))`, where `n = [K : k]`: the closed point `[α : 1]` for a primitive
element `α` of `K`, cut out by the homogenized minimal polynomial of `α`. -/
theorem exists_effectiveCartierDivisor_isoSpec_picardClassOf_eq
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [Algebra k K] [FiniteDimensional k K] [Algebra.IsSeparable k K] :
    ∃ (D : (Stacks.Chow.bundle (Stacks.SymGraded.freeModule (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k))
        (Stacks.SymGraded.coordIndex.{u} 1))).IdealSheafData)
      (hD : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D)
      (e : D.subscheme ≅ Spec (CommRingCat.of K)),
      e.hom ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)) =
          D.subschemeι ≫ Stacks.Chow.bundleProj (Stacks.SymGraded.freeModule
            (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (Stacks.SymGraded.coordIndex.{u} 1)) ∧
        Stacks.WeilCohomology.picardClassOf _ (Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheaf D)
            (haveI := hD; inferInstance) =
          (Module.finrank k K : ℤ) • Stacks.WeilCohomology.picardClassOf _
            (Stacks.Chow.bundleTwist (Stacks.SymGraded.freeModule
              (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (Stacks.SymGraded.coordIndex.{u} 1)))
            (Stacks.Chow.isInvertible_bundleTwist (Stacks.SymGraded.freeModule
              (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (Stacks.SymGraded.coordIndex.{u} 1))) := by
  let pb := Field.powerBasisOfFiniteOfSeparable k K
  refine ⟨bundleDivisor pb, inferInstance, bundleDivisorIso pb, bundleDivisorIso_hom_comp pb, ?_⟩
  have hdeg : ((deg pb • 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) = (Module.finrank k K : ℤ) := by
    rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_one, deg, pb.natDegree_minpoly, pb.finrank]
  exact (picardClassOf_divisorSheaf_bundleDivisor pb).trans
    (congrArg (· • picardClassOf _ (Stacks.Chow.bundleTwist (freeRankTwo k))
      (Stacks.Chow.isInvertible_bundleTwist (freeRankTwo k))) hdeg)

end Stacks.WeilCohomology

end
